<mxCell id="math" value="a = QACT(e + P[n,j])      then      X⁽⁰⁾ = QACT(a + E[m,j])&lt;br&gt;QACT = round to nearest, ties to even, then clip to the stored activation range." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#374151;fontColor=#374151;strokeWidth=2;rounded=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#263442;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="450" width="990" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note" value="A is the current ACT value; B is a trained parameter. Fraction alignment uses exact shifts and extra bits, not early rounding.&lt;br&gt;Each addition returns one converted result; the stage controller owns memory reads and writes. Addition FSM: Page 5.&lt;br&gt;Saturation is recorded but does not stop the frame. No multiplication, division, normalization or dot product is needed here." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#374151;fontColor=#374151;strokeWidth=2;rounded=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#263442;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="615" width="1440" height="85" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
